  "summary": "The study compares three self-supporting Ti3C2Tx electrodes prepared from LiF/HCl-etched MXene: a dense vacuum-filtered Ti3C2Tx-film control, a liquid-nitrogen-rapid-frozen 3d-Ti3C2Tx-film, and a directly frozen aerogel. All products were annealed under Ar at 673 K and evaluated in 3 M H2SO4 after pressing at 10 MPa. The aerogel showed the largest reported gravimetric capacitance, 414 F g\u22121 at 1 mV s\u22121, while the headline 3d-Ti3C2Tx-film provided the highest reported GCD volumetric capacitance, 1355 F cm\u22123 at 1 A g\u22121, and was used for the symmetric device. Mass loading, areal capacitance, quantitative porosity, tortuosity, and lateral flake dimensions were not reported."
}